    "steps": [
      "Whisk the hazelnut meal and sugar with the baking powder, sea salt, baking soda and black pepper in a large bowl until evenly mixed with no sugar lumps.",
      "Add the beaten egg, melted butter, extract, chopped chocolate and crystallized ginger. Stir with a wooden spoon until everything holds together as one dough.",
      "Rub a little neutral oil on your hands and roll the dough into 12 equal balls. Press each ball into a 2-inch (5 cm) disc.",
      "Set the discs on a parchment-lined baking sheet and wrap the sheet tightly in plastic. Freeze until firm, at least 10 minutes and ideally 2 hours.",
      "Heat the oven to 350°F (180°C). Cover another baking sheet with a layer of parchment.",
      "Move 6 discs to the fresh sheet and space the cookies well apart on both. Keep one sheet in the fridge while the other bakes.",
      "Bake one sheet at a time at 350°F (180°C) for 12–15 minutes, until the cookies are golden brown.",
      "Transfer the cookies to a wire rack and leave them until completely cool.",
      "You nailed it! Grab a plate and dig in."
